<article class="env-lemma" id="0AWY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AWY">Lemma <span data-tag="0AWY">47.23.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring. If $A$ has a dualizing complex, then the formal fibres of $A$ are Gorenstein. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime of $A$. The formal fibre of $A$ at $\mathfrak p$ is isomorphic to the formal fibre of $A/\mathfrak p$ at $(0)$. The quotient $A/\mathfrak p$ has a dualizing complex (Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7I" data-tag="0A7I">47.15.9</a>). Thus it suffices to check the statement when $A$ is a local domain and $\mathfrak p = (0)$. Let $\omega _ A^\bullet $ be a dualizing complex for $A$. Then $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A A^\wedge $ is a dualizing complex for the completion $A^\wedge $ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0AWD" data-tag="0AWD">47.22.1</a>). Then $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A K$ is a dualizing complex for the fraction field $K$ of $A$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7G" data-tag="0A7G">47.15.6</a>). Hence $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A K$ is isomorphic to $K[n]$ for some $n \in \mathbf{Z}$. Similarly, we conclude a dualizing complex for the formal fibre $A^\wedge \otimes _ A K$ is 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A A^\wedge \otimes _{A^\wedge } (A^\wedge \otimes _ A K) = (\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A K) \otimes _ K (A^\wedge \otimes _ A K) \cong (A^\wedge \otimes _ A K)[n]  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>